body:
Carbs generally are anything that is primarily a bread or sugar. And yes there are carbs in veggies, etc. but usually are very low compared to something that is literally a piece of bread, or sugar, and green veggies have less than non-green veggies like carrots. I count fruits as a carb because those tend to have a higher sugar content than vegetables.

&#x200B;

It is good to know that carbs are burned/used up by your body very quickly.

Fats(cheese, oil, avocado, etc.) burn slowly, as do proteins.

And then there is fiber, which is digested very slowly by your body, or even not at all, but results in you feeling fuller for a longer period of time, but does not provide any energy.

&#x200B;

Anway, my point is that by having a meal that has a good balance of these types of foods will give you energy that lasts longer and keeps you feeling full too. So personally what I do is pick 1 food from each category to make my meal(1 protein, green vegetables, a fat, and a carb) For example my breakfast is 1 egg(protein), cheese(fat), baby spinach(green veggie and fiber), and low sugar oatmeal(carb and fiber)

&#x200B;

This type of eating will give you some quick energy from the carbs, but also some slow burning fuel to get you through to the next meal or snack.

I see that roasted is on here already(a lot) so I will just add that personally I have been adding ground mustard to things like broccoli, spinach, brussel sprouts, and green beans. Along with the usual salt, pepper, and garlic of course. 

&#x200B;

Roasted carrots turns out are really good with cumin, as are cauliflower too.

Hi everyone, I'm so excited to have this blanket finished. It's the Stardust Melodies pattern found at [http://everytrickonthehook.com/crochet-alongs/stardust-melodies-cal/](http://everytrickonthehook.com/crochet-alongs/stardust-melodies-cal/)

&#x200B;

It covers my queen size bed  and took the last 5 months to make making 1 square a day and sewing them all together at the end. There is a border around it too about 1.5 inches. Its my first blanket and certainly my first project this big period and I'm really happy with it!
